1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:03,220
谢谢 这儿有位安德鲁·杰克逊[20美元]
Hey, thank you. Here's an Andrew Jackson.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:04,730
给我弄一床干净的被单
Make a clean set of sheets happen,

3
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:06,820
我就把你介绍给他双胞胎兄弟
I'll introduce you to his twin brother.

4
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:10,010
其实不用非得逗她 不过我又不会少块肉对吧
You don't have to do the banter, but what's it cost me?

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:12,580
曼尼 坐火车这主意太棒了
Manny, it was a great idea to come on the train.

6
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,510
铁路是体面旅行的最后一道堡垒了
Rail is a last bastion of respectable travel

7
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:17,050
现在机场真的是什么样的人都能去了
now that every airport has become a sweat-pant convention.

8
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:18,770
我们全家要去波特兰
We are all traveling to Portland

9
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:22,180
因为杰的前妻迪迪要再婚了
because Jay's ex-wife, Dede, is getting remarried.

10
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:23,110
我们好开心
We're so happy.

11
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:24,230
是为我们自己
For us.

12
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,340
这意味着我不用再付该死的赡养费了
It means the end of those damn alimony payments,

13
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:28,340
所以我要确保迪迪顺利完婚
so I'm gonna make sure Dede goes through with it.

14
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:31,920
只要"我愿意""我愿意""结束了"
It'll be, "I do", "I do", "I'm done".

15
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,110
兄弟 我们这趟火车上得做多少次抉择啊
Dude, how much choice action are we gonna get on this trip?

16
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:38,210
我正在调整我的期待值
I'm managing my expectations.

17
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:40,090
你一点也不了解火车吗
Don't you know anything about trains?

18
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:41,470
姑娘们都变疯了
Chicks go crazy.

19
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:43,260
颠簸会让她们兴奋
The vibrations get them all worked up.

20
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:45,310
而且她们无处可去 正好下手
Also, they're trapped, which is nice.

21
00:00:46,390 --> 00:00:48,400
我们要去写给老妈的祝酒辞
We're just gonna go bang out this toast for Mom.

22
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:49,810
是啊 不能拖到最后再写
Yeah. Shouldn't have waited till the last minute.

23
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:52,100
正好可以让你分心 免得晕车
It'll be a nice distraction from your motion sickness.

24
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,790
没关系 只要火车前进时
It's good, as long as I'm not facing backwards

25
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:56,580
我不是背对着...天哪 不行
when the train is -- Oh, God, no.

26
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:57,560
带我走
Lead me.

27
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,700
好 我来吧
All right, I got it.

28
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,660
走吧 固定点
There you go. Fixed point.

29
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:15,950
我的天哪 不是吧
Oh, my God, it can't be.

30
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,250
什么 不是啦 不是秃头啦
What? No, it's not a bald spot.

31
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:18,700
我昨天晚上没睡好
I slept on it funny last night.

32
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,050
不是啦 两排后的那个家伙
No. The guy two rows back.

33
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,990
那是西蒙·黑
That's Simon Ha--

34
00:01:22,990 --> 00:01:24,450
黑斯廷斯 我的...
Hastings. Oh, my --

35
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:25,440
你也是他粉丝吗
You're a fan of his, too?

36
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,850
他是我最喜欢的作家
He's my favorite author.

37
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:27,990
别告诉米奇尔 我读他上一本书的时候
Don't tell Mitchell, but I was so engrossed

38
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,690
因为太投入 有一天半忘了喂莉莉
in his last book, I didn't feed Lily for a day and a half.

39
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:33,620
等等
Wait a second.

40
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:36,900
西蒙·黑斯廷斯是
Simon Hastings is the genius behind

41
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,840
《锡尔弗敦》系列悬疑小说的天才作者
the Silverton mystery novels.

42
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,050
《仅限非会员》
"Dismembers Only."

43
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:41,210
《新鲜空气之死》
"A Death of Fresh Air."

44
00:01:41,210 --> 00:01:42,150
全世界等
The world has been waiting

45
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:43,440
三部曲的最后一部
for the final book of the trilogy

46
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,760
得有10年了吧
for almost, what, 10 years?

47
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:47,050
我太迫不及待了 自己先写了同人小说
I missed it so much, I took a stab at writing fan fiction.

48
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:48,000
什么
What?

49
00:01:48,090 --> 00:01:50,200
我把锡尔弗敦置身于房地产的悲惨世界
I put Silverton in the harrowing world of real estate

50
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,810
名字就叫《开放日·密闭之棺》
with "Open House, Closed Casket."

51
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:55,040
起鸡皮疙瘩了
Goose bumps.

52
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:03,710
很抱歉打扰您 但是您是我们最爱的作家
We hate to bother you, but you are our favorite author.

53
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:05,970
先生们 文字都是现成的
Gentlemen, the words are all out there.

54
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:09,080
我只是按能赚钱的方式排布了一下而已
I just arrange them in a financially rewarding way.

55
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,520
-滑稽 太滑稽了 -典型的黑斯廷斯
- Droll. Droll is what it is. - Classic Hastings.

56
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:13,760
您现在是在...
That by any chance isn't the --

57
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,410
写下一部锡尔弗敦的小说吗
the next Silverton novel, is it?

58
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:17,330
你们是说《云霄火车杀人事件》吗
You mean "Locomotive for Murder"?

59
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:18,390
太妙了
Crackerjack.

60
00:02:18,390 --> 00:02:20,490
都还没出呢 我已经在为要读完它而伤感了
It's not even out yet, and I'm sad about finishing it.

61
00:02:20,490 --> 00:02:22,520
希望不会让你们失望
Well, I hope you won't be disappointed.

62
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,790
很高兴认识你们
Lovely to meet you.

63
00:02:27,330 --> 00:02:28,010
你一般是怎么写作的
What's your process?

64
00:02:28,010 --> 00:02:29,610
人物只是通过你说话吗
Are the characters just speaking through you?

65
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,180
情节有多重要呢
How important is plot?

66
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:33,990
这样吧 你们安静地坐下来
Here's an idea -- how would you two like

67
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:36,780
读一读第一章怎么样
to sit quietly and read the first chapter?

68
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:37,990
什么
What?

69
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:39,450
-我的... -什么
- My... - What?

70
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:41,050
-天哪 -什么
- God. - What?

71
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:42,540
请放心
Rest assured.

72
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:44,090
我们会保护好您的宝贝
Your treasure is in good hands.

73
00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:46,600
我们也是在艺术界混的
We are also members of the artistic community.

74
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,440
我是小丑
Clown.

75
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,330
我是魔术师
Magician.

76
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:53,210
不行
Nope.

77
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,550
为什么 我们在火车上
What? We're on a train,

78
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:56,580
我在享受这种浪漫的旅行方式啊
and I'm embracing a romantic style of travel.

79
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,190
我懂 我爱死了
I get it, and I love it.

80
00:02:58,190 --> 00:02:59,830
维多利亚饮茶帽真不错
Wonderful Victorian tea hat.

81
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:01,830
谢谢 一流的旅行德比帽
Thank you. Top-notch travel derby.

82
00:03:01,830 --> 00:03:03,810
女士 下午茶见
Ma'am. See you at high tea.

83
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:06,750
他的样子太娘了
He acts like someone with low "T".

84
00:03:07,110 --> 00:03:09,630
我买口香糖的时候落了我的杂志了
Ugh, I forgot my magazines when I was buying gum.

85
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:11,480
一心两用实在太难了吧
Oh, it's hard to do two things at once.

86
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,800
你还有书吗
You got an extra book?

87
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,880
我在重读《简·爱》
Well, I'm re-reading "Jane Eyre",

88
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,850
但我行李架上还有本《安娜·卡列尼娜》
but I've got "Anna Karenina" on deck.

89
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,030
你的是什么
What you got?

90
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:19,140
《哈丽特飓风》 基本都是图片
"Hurricane Harriet". It's mostly pictures.

91
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:20,660
成交 你坐过去
Sold. Move over.

92
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:23,690
哈丽特是干嘛的
So, what's Harriet's deal?

93
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:25,950
她是个没头没脑的傻姑娘 总给人惹麻烦
She's a ditzy girl who causes problems for everyone,

94
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:27,490
但自己从来都不知道
but never realizes it.

95
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,620
听起来不太现实啊
Doesn't sound very realistic.

96
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,510
你们知道厕所在哪儿吗
Ah, do you guys know where the bathroom is?

97
00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:35,720
在后面
Oh, back there.

98
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:37,220
不是那边吗
Isn't it that way?

99
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,180
没关系啦
Doesn't matter.

100
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:43,550
请出示头等座票
First-class ticket, please.

101
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:44,650
我只是来找厕所的
I just came looking for the bathroom.

102
00:03:44,650 --> 00:03:45,900
我的票在我的座位上
My ticket is in my seat.

103
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,140
你知道我每天会听到多少人说这种话吗
Do you have any idea how many times a day I hear that?

104
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,690
坐回原位[回到自己的国家]去
Just go back where you came from.

105
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:51,360
叫我回去
Go back where I came from?

106
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:52,520
好吧
Okay.

107
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,940
我明白了
I see how it is.

108
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:05,960
所以哈丽特傻不愣登地把那些人送进熊洞了吗
So, Harriet just sent those people right into a bear cave?

109
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:07,930
她永远不知道自己在干什么
She never knows what she's doing.

110
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,710
好傻啊
What an idiot.

111
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,270
打扰一下
Excuse me.

112
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:16,700
介意我坐这儿吗
You mind if I sit here?

113
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,260
不啊
Uh, no.

114
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,250
你的笑容很美
You have a beautiful smile.

115
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:24,090
谢谢
Thanks.

116
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,830
大家都嘲笑我的帽子
They make fun of you for wearing your headgear,

117
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,990
但是现在看看吧
but, hey, look at me now.

118
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:29,790
出示一下票
Tickets?

119
00:04:29,930 --> 00:04:30,850
是啊
Oh, yeah.

120
00:04:30,850 --> 00:04:32,930
亲爱的 我的票在你那里吗
Uh, honey, do you have my ticket?

121
00:04:32,930 --> 00:04:33,470
没有啊
No.

122
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,520
我很肯定我把我的票给你了 宝贝
I'm pretty sure I gave you my ticket, babe.

123
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,730
抱歉 宝贝 回站票车厢去
Sorry, babe. Back to coach.

124
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:38,580
我原谅你
I forgive you.

125
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,010
来找我
Come find me.

126
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,570
老妈一向自由自在无拘无束
"Mom has always been a free spirit."

127
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:54,740
她也帮忙释放了酒瓶里的冤魂
"She has also helped to free a lot of spirits from bottles

128
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:57,010
因为这女人是个酒鬼 记好咯
'cause the woman's a boozehound!" Hello!

129
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:58,210
我不会写这个的
Yeah, I'm not gonna put that in.

130
00:04:58,210 --> 00:04:59,340
这个怎么样
Uh, how about this one?

131
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:00,930
她的巧克力豆饼干的秘诀是
"The secret to her chocolate chip cookies

132
00:05:00,930 --> 00:05:02,300
撒一小撮盐
was a dash of salt --"

133
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:06,770
和两大勺疯狂 因为这位女士心态失衡
"And two scoops of crazy because the lady's imbalanced."

134
00:05:06,770 --> 00:05:07,550
记好咯
Hello!

135
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:09,320
克莱尔 是要祝福她 不是要苛责她
Claire, this is toast, not a roast.

136
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:12,000
你不舒服是因为这是你这辈子
Are you uncomfortable because, for the first time in your life,

137
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,910
第一次要变直[率]了吗
you have to be the straight man?

138
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:14,550
记好咯
Hello!

139
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:17,010
老说"记好咯"也不会让挖苦人的话变有趣的
Saying "Hello" doesn't make mean things funny.

140
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:18,000
我喜欢
I like it.

141
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:18,830
做决定的又不是你
Well, you don't get to decide.

142
00:05:18,830 --> 00:05:19,930
为什么是你
How come you get to decide?

143
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:21,180
因为妈妈让我说祝酒词 不是你
'Cause Mom asked me and not you.

144
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:23,390
叫你来是因为我有负罪感
I included you because I felt bad.

145
00:05:26,090 --> 00:05:27,330
好吧 我不在乎
That's fine. I don't care.

146
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:28,930
你自己搞定吧
You can do it yourself.

147
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,500
-我不在意 -克莱尔
- I don't care. - Claire.

148
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:32,820
等等
Wait.

149
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:34,590
不
Nope.

150
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,560
给你20块
This is a $20.

151
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:37,710
待会我妻子来了之后
When my wife shows up later,

152
00:05:37,710 --> 00:05:39,880
"冰茶"就是威士忌的代号
"Iced tea" means Scotch.

153
00:05:41,130 --> 00:05:42,620
外公 你会不会觉得外婆请你
Grandpa, do you think it's weird

154
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:44,190
参加她的婚礼很奇怪
Nana invited you to her wedding?

155
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:46,480
我觉得这是有史以来迪迪做出的最正常的事
I think it's the least-weird thing Dede's ever done.

156
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,310
如果她那么糟糕 你为什么还娶她
Well, if she was so bad, why'd you ever marry her?

157
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:49,420
我们当时都很年轻
We were young.

158
00:05:49,610 --> 00:05:52,850
她很漂亮 但她一直疯个没完
She was cute, but the constant nuttiness of Dede

159
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:55,770
把我累坏了 简直都不想活了
wore me down, robbed me of my will to live.

160
00:05:55,990 --> 00:05:57,350
有一天 她把我逼得受不了了
One day, she pushed me off the edge.

161
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,450
我从家里跑了出来
I ran out of the house.

162
00:05:58,450 --> 00:06:01,080
他们在当地消防局找到了裸身的我
They found me shirtless in the local fire station.

163
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:01,950
不好意思
Excuse me.

164
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:04,000
你说的这位迪迪
This, uh, Dede that you're speaking of --

165
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,560
是不是迪迪·普里契特
um, is that Dede Pritchett, by chance?

166
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,570
你认识她吗
Do you know her?

167
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,380
她要嫁的人是我父亲
She's marrying my father.

168
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:11,110
不会吧
You're kidding.

169
00:06:11,150 --> 00:06:13,380
真的 我们就是在去婚礼的路上
No. We're traveling to the wedding right now...

170
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:14,790
如果还会有婚礼的话
if there is one.

171
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:16,350
我得给爸打个电话
I've got to call Dad.

172
00:06:16,350 --> 00:06:18,510
我早说了那女人不正常
I told you that woman was off.

173
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:22,270
小费还是改成2块好了
I'm gonna need $18 back.

174
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:25,370
不好意思
Uh, excuse me.

175
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:26,410
你好 海斯廷斯先生
Uh, hi, Mr. Hastings.

176
00:06:26,410 --> 00:06:29,270
你知不知道 有没有开发出一种药
Um, do you know -- have they developed a cure yet?

177
00:06:29,270 --> 00:06:29,860
治什么用的
For what?

178
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:33,340
破碎的心灵 因为我们俩的心都爽炸了
A blown mind -- because we have two of them.

179
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:34,140
你们太好了
You're too kind.

180
00:06:34,150 --> 00:06:35,590
-谢谢 -谢谢
- Oh, thank you. - Oh, thank you.

181
00:06:35,590 --> 00:06:38,410
我们就是超想知道列车长是怎么
Well, we are just dying to know how the conductor got

182
00:06:38,410 --> 00:06:41,040
从车头来到车尾杀了大使
all the way from the front to the back, kill the ambassador,

183
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,290
还不被人发现的
and not be seen?

184
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:45,450
控制室有一个应急出口
There's an escape hatch in the control room.

185
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:47,570
他爬上去 从列车顶部
He climbs up, crawls his way across

186
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:49,430
爬到守车
the top of the train to the caboose.

187
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:53,880
他穿了磁性鞋 双脚牢牢吸在车顶
There, his feet firmly planted, thanks to magnetic shoes,

188
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:56,160
他倒挂着身子 向大使开枪
he hangs down, shoots the ambassador,

189
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:58,160
再按原路爬了回去
then crawls back the way he came.

190
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:00,250
太巧妙了
That is so ingenious.

191
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:01,950
他是怎么没被摄像头拍到的
How does he avoid the video cameras?

192
00:07:01,950 --> 00:07:03,320
-对啊 -你说什么
- Yeah. - I beg your pardon.

193
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,500
车顶上的
On top of the train.

194
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:06,670
他坐的火车没装摄像头
He's on a train that doesn't have any cameras.

195
00:07:06,670 --> 00:07:09,060
现在的火车都有了 老大
Oh, no, they all have cameras now -- Big Brother.

196
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,740
我刚在《铁路世界》的一篇文章上看到的
I just read an article about it in Rail World,

197
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:12,300
就是你座位口袋里那本杂志
the magazine in your seat pocket --

198
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:14,210
还看了一篇对业余列车长凡莱丽·柏帝内的采访
also a great interview with amateur conductor

199
00:07:14,210 --> 00:07:15,330
写得可好了
Valerie Bertinelli.

200
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:17,770
如果这是真的 那谋杀不可能完成
Well, if that's true, then the murder isn't possible.

201
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,480
如果大使还活着
And if the ambassador is still alive,

202
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,600
锡尔弗顿就没理由去尼日利亚
then there's no reason for Silverton to be in Nigeria.

203
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,740
要是这样的话 他就不会参加行动
And if that's the case, he's not at the coup,

204
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:28,570
也就是说整件事都行不通了
which means the whole thing doesn't work.

205
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:31,060
我的上帝 我没法出书了
Dear God, I have no book.

206
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:36,310
我没法出书了
I have no book!

207
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,550
好后悔我还把错字圈出来了
Now I wish I hadn't circled the typos.

208
00:07:41,530 --> 00:07:44,210
我还在这做什么 去找他呀
What are you still doing here? Go find him.

209
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:45,410
我不知道
I don't know.

210
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:46,650
快去啊 这个爱情故事
Come on, it's a better love story

211
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:48,000
比你看的要精彩
than the one you're reading.

212
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,250
你美丽 高贵 聪明
You're the beautiful, high-class, smart girl,

213
00:07:50,250 --> 00:07:52,780
而他是个穷小子 跟一群流浪汉
and he's the poor boy duct-taping his shoes

214
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:54,270
以车厢为家
with a bunch of hobos in coach.

215
00:07:54,270 --> 00:07:55,600
票价也就差20块
It's a $20 difference.

216
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,490
艾丽克斯 你能行的
Alex, you got this.

217
00:07:57,490 --> 00:07:59,000
男生为火车疯狂
Trains make guys crazy.

218
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,290
你什么时候坐过火车
When were you ever on a train?

219
00:08:00,290 --> 00:08:03,040
在拉斯维加斯 我坐火车去取的行李
In Vegas, between my plane and the luggage area.

220
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,260
被托运到别的地方去了
Stuff went down.

221
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:05,180
好吧 我去了
Fine. I'll go for it.

222
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,070
等等
Oh, wait.

223
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,160
别戴帽子
Nope.

224
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,610
曼尼喜欢戴帽子 对吧
Manny likes hats, doesn't he?

225
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:16,900
某人还对他有好感哦
Ooh, someone's still got a crush.

226
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,290
我并不以此为傲
I'm not proud of it.

227
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:19,660
试过要放下的
I tried to get past it.

228
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:21,110
不过 火车嘛 你懂的
But, you know, trains.

229
00:08:21,110 --> 00:08:24,410
我觉得你看着挺可爱的 他应该也会这么想
Well, I think you look cute, and I bet he would, too.

230
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:27,240
嘿 小色鬼们
Hey, pervs.

231
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:29,470
我猜猜 钓妹子钓得肩膀都酸了吧
Let me guess -- shoulders tired from striking out so hard?

232
00:08:29,470 --> 00:08:30,830
时间还早呢
It's still early.

233
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:34,000
我看到一枚十分硬币
Ooh, I see a dime piece over there.

234
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,170
就是说她是个十分妹子
That means she's a 10.

235
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:36,440
我知道 我也会说暗语
Yeah. I speak d-bag.

236
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,780
卢克 她年纪有点大吧
Luke, she's a little old.

237
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:40,000
詹妮弗·洛佩兹都快90岁了
Hey, Jennifer Lopez is like 90.

238
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,740
我偶尔还会把抱枕想象成她呢
Doesn't mean I don't pretend she's my pillow every now and then.

239
00:08:44,050 --> 00:08:45,460
怎么会有妹子看上他呢
How does he have prospects?

240
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,560
希望你能好受些
If it makes you feel any better,

241
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,440
那边的小家伙可喜欢你了
that one's got a big crush on you.

242
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:54,330
我并该感到不意外
I guess I shouldn't have been surprised.

243
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:56,730
我总能感觉到艾丽克斯对我的些许热情
I've always sensed a little heat from Alex.

244
00:08:56,730 --> 00:08:58,490
女人要是不想钻进男人的外套
A woman doesn't compliment a man on his hat

245
00:08:58,490 --> 00:09:00,320
怎么会称赞他的帽子呢
unless she wants to get into his blazer.

246
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:04,510
和好吧
Peace offering?

247
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:05,460
多谢
Thank you.

248
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,560
听着 很抱歉我跟你说
Look, I'm sorry I told you

249
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:08,720
妈妈选我致祝酒词而不是你
that Mom picked me for the toast and not you.

250
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,980
我只是觉得
It's just that

251
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:11,770
我和她一直有一种很特殊的联系
I've always had a special relationship with her.

252
00:09:11,770 --> 00:09:14,350
当然了 就像女巫和飞猴的关系一样
Sure, like the one between a witch and her flying monkey.

253
00:09:14,350 --> 00:09:14,920
别这样
Don't do that.

254
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,770
别用《绿野仙踪》酸我
Don't use "The Wizard of Oz" against me.

255
00:09:16,770 --> 00:09:18,260
妈妈爱摆布你
Mom manipulates you.

256
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:20,080
她利用你来对付我们其他人
She uses you against the rest of us.

257
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,690
真不知道你在说什么
I have no idea what you're talking about.

258
00:09:21,690 --> 00:09:23,880
天 我想个例子
Oh, God, if only I could think of an example.

259
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:25,600
等等 这是三十个例子之一
Oh, wait, here's one of 30.

260
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:28,160
她翘了艾丽克斯的毕业典礼却没告诉我们
She blew off Alex's graduation, but she didn't tell us.

261
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:28,830
她逼你来说
She made you do it

262
00:09:28,830 --> 00:09:31,370
这样我们所有人就都会指责你而不是她
so we would all dump on you instead of her.

263
00:09:31,370 --> 00:09:34,570
这次她不让我致祝酒词
And now she bans me from giving a toast,

264
00:09:34,570 --> 00:09:36,060
我们俩却在为此争执
and we're fighting about it.

265
00:09:36,070 --> 00:09:37,910
得了吧 她把你当肉盾利用
Come on. She's using you like a human shield.

266
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,690
这算是健康的关系吗
Does that seem like a healthy relationship?

267
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:41,760
好好想想吧
Why don't you give that some thought

268
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,050
顺便再给我倒一杯来
while you're getting me a refill?

269
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:43,950
你什么时候喝光的
When did you even drink that?

270
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:45,740
明明一直在说话
You've been talking the whole time.

271
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:48,140
好吧 根本没信号
Fine. I don't get anything.

272
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:49,710
别 伙计
No... Hey, pal.

273
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:50,860
先别给你爸打电话
Before you call your dad,

274
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,490
我刚才关于迪迪的言论
what I was saying about Dede

275
00:09:52,490 --> 00:09:54,630
只是在掩饰而已 因为我失去了
was me just covering up because I lost

276
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:57,770
最美好 最持重的人
the greatest, most stable person I've ever known.

277
00:09:57,770 --> 00:09:59,170
可你看上去很生气
But you seemed so angry.

278
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:00,690
因为我放不下她
It's because I can't get over her.

279
00:10:00,690 --> 00:10:01,740
我试了所有方法
I've tried everything --

280
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:03,530
理疗 吃药 电击
therapy, pills, electricity.

281
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:04,750
对不起
I'm sorry.

282
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:06,130
我只是太想她了
It's just that I miss her so much.

283
00:10:06,130 --> 00:10:08,540
我将见到世界上最幸运的男人
I-I'm gonna see the luckiest man in the world

284
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,300
迎娶世界上最美好的女人
marry the most wonderful woman in the world,

285
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:11,640
而我却孤身一人
and I have nobody.

286
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:13,180
不好意思 先生
Excuse me, sir.

287
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:15,130
这位女士说她是你妻子
This woman says she's your wife.

288
00:10:15,130 --> 00:10:16,310
我不认识她
Never seen her before.

289
00:10:17,890 --> 00:10:21,070
但我认识这位 我儿子 米奇尔
But here's someone I do know -- my son, Mitchell.

290
00:10:21,070 --> 00:10:22,660
米奇尔和迪迪是密友
Mitchell and Dede are great pals.

291
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:24,600
给这些朋友介绍一下你妈妈
Tell these lovely folks about your mother.

292
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,860
她是个腹黑的女魔头
She's a scheming dragon woman

293
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:27,760
拼命摧毁她身边的所有人
hell-bent on destroying everyone around her.

294
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,210
你一定要选在今天觉悟吗
You pick today to realize that?!

295
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:29,900
不客气
You're welcome.

296
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:31,070
我终于让他看清了
I finally got him to see Mom

297
00:10:31,070 --> 00:10:34,360
妈妈真正的样子 险恶的老疯子
for who she really is -- a nasty, old nutjob.

298
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,310
但她现在是其他人的烦恼了
But she's someone else's problem now, huh?

299
00:10:36,310 --> 00:10:37,270
等一下 你知道吗
Wait a minute. You know what?

300
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:38,990
我也不认识这些人
I don't know these people, either.

301
00:10:39,010 --> 00:10:39,940
走吧 失陪
Let's go. Excuse me.

302
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:40,870
失陪
Pardon us.

303
00:10:42,490 --> 00:10:43,650
你好 我叫海莉
Hi. I'm Haley.

304
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:45,580
很高兴见到你 我是个大骗子
Pleasure. I'm a massive fraud.

305
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,110
听起来你需要喝一杯
Sounds like you need a drink.

306
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,510
我不觉得那是个好主意
I'm not sure that's a good idea.

307
00:10:48,510 --> 00:10:49,170
我以前会用...
I used to have something of a...

308
00:10:49,170 --> 00:10:51,770
来嘛 我觉得一个人喝很奇怪
Oh, come on. I feel weird drinking alone.

309
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:54,200
我不觉得 我只是想让他买单
I don't. I just wanted him to pay.

310
00:10:54,590 --> 00:10:56,160
上一次我喝那么醉的时候
The last time I was this bladdered,

311
00:10:56,160 --> 00:11:00,790
我暴揍了萨曼·拉什迪那个自命不凡的家伙
I parked my fist right in Salman Rushdie's smug gob.

312
00:11:01,770 --> 00:11:03,320
你知道阿黛尔吗
Do you know Adele?

313
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:07,590
-他在这里 -过来看一眼
- There he is. - Hey. Just checking in. Hi.

314
00:11:07,590 --> 00:11:09,250
在庆祝自己解决了难题吗
Ooh, celebrating solving your problem?

315
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:12,380
在才思枯竭中煎熬了十年之后
After 10 years of paralyzing writer's block,

316
00:11:12,390 --> 00:11:13,730
我以为自己终于能够
I at last felt that I was drinking

317
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:16,310
直接获得灵感缪斯的哺育
directly from the teat of the muse.

318
00:11:16,310 --> 00:11:17,710
但她不是缪斯
But she was no muse.

319
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,030
她是妖魔
She was a succubus.

320
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:20,830
真有语言天分
Such a gift for language.

321
00:11:20,830 --> 00:11:23,940
在下一站 我就要烧掉这本书
At the next stop, I'm going to burn this book.

322
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:24,980
太有种了
That is bad-ass.

323
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,170
不 什么
No! What?

324
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,420
是的 这将会是我职业生涯的最后一笔
Yes. It will be the last act of my career.

325
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:32,310
别算上在波特兰的专题讨论会
Well, not counting the panel discussion in Portland.

326
00:11:32,310 --> 00:11:33,320
取消掉就太无礼了
It would be rude to cancel.

327
00:11:33,330 --> 00:11:34,910
招待会上有葡萄酒和奶酪
There's a wine-and-cheese reception.

328
00:11:34,910 --> 00:11:36,640
你必须写完它
You have to finish.

329
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:39,290
如果我们能证明它可行呢
What if we proved it could happen?

330
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:40,480
也许还有别的方法
Maybe there's another way

331
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:43,300
能让杀人犯去到最后一节车厢再回来
for the murderer to get to the caboose and back.

332
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:45,130
火车上全都是
I've filled the train with characters

333
00:11:45,130 --> 00:11:47,410
无法知道工程师留下邮件的角色
who cannot know that the engineer has left his post.

334
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:48,880
没有希望了
It's hopeless!

335
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,840
等等 我们停下来了吗
Wait. Did we just stop?

336
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:52,450
-不 我不觉得 -没有
- No. I don't think so. - No. Mnh-mnh.

337
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,590
看看加利福尼亚多美呀
Look how beautiful California is.

338
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:03,290
乘坐火车最美妙的地方
The best part about taking the train,

339
00:12:03,290 --> 00:12:06,820
就像我常常跟 孩子们说的一样
as I often do for my work with, uh, the children,

340
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:08,500
就是风景了
has got to be the scenery.

341
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,420
是吗
Yeah?

342
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,450
你最喜欢的景点是哪里
What's your favorite spot?

343
00:12:10,450 --> 00:12:13,560
我觉得必须是...
Well, I'd have to say the spot where, uh...

344
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,960
格兰德河倾入苏必利尔湖的景色
the Rio Grande pours into Lake Superior.

345
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:18,570
我好像没见过
Huh. I don't think I've seen that.

346
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:20,350
能容许我失陪一小会吗
Can you excuse me for just a pinch?

347
00:12:20,350 --> 00:12:21,080
当然
Sure.

348
00:12:28,570 --> 00:12:29,680
你在干嘛
What are you doing?

349
00:12:29,870 --> 00:12:32,720
让自己变得丰盈 那样才能更进一步
Getting swollen 'cause that's how you close.

350
00:12:32,950 --> 00:12:34,570
顺便说一句
Oh, by the way,

351
00:12:34,570 --> 00:12:37,490
要是一条领带挂在门前 那就是卢克开始得分了
if you see a tie on our door, Luke's starting to score.

352
00:12:37,810 --> 00:12:39,720
现在就为你加油有点困难
It's a little hard to root for you right now.

353
00:12:41,310 --> 00:12:43,260
我们说到哪了
So, where were we?

354
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,970
这是你第一次来大苏尔海岸线吗
Is this your first time seeing the Central Coast, Big Sur?

355
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:48,120
不 不是的 小姐
No, it's not, little miss.

356
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,780
我等不及要观赏今晚安第斯山脉上的日落了
I can't wait to watch the sunset over the Andes tonight.

357
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:54,540
虽然现在我面前的景色也很秀美
Not like my view right now isn't fantastic.

358
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,750
你很可爱
You're cute.

359
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:58,110
如果你喜欢
You know, if you're into it,

360
00:12:58,110 --> 00:13:00,890
我想我可以给你看点东西
I think I could show you a few things.

361
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:04,400
这里有点吵
Uh... It's a little loud in here.

362
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,610
也许我们该去个安静的地方
Maybe we should go somewhere more quiet.

363
00:13:06,610 --> 00:13:07,520
没问题
Sure.

364
00:13:07,810 --> 00:13:08,630
真的吗
Really?

365
00:13:10,190 --> 00:13:11,310
火车
Trains.

366
00:13:14,770 --> 00:13:16,210
你很专注
You're so serious.

367
00:13:16,610 --> 00:13:18,510
我想尽可能地画出你的美
I want to make sure I capture your beauty.

368
00:13:18,510 --> 00:13:19,540
我可以看看吗
Can I see yet?

369
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:20,670
希望你喜欢
I hope you like it.

370
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,780
他不是艺术家 谁在乎呢
So, he's not an artist. Who cares?

371
00:13:35,970 --> 00:13:37,880
头等舱的人以为
People in first class think they have it made

372
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:41,370
提早登舱和稍稍干净一点的座位就代表着成功
with their early boarding and their slightly cleaner seats.

373
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:45,220
但他们不懂生活
But they don't know what living is.

374
00:13:54,870 --> 00:13:56,580
我愿为上卫生间排长队
I'll take a long line for the bathroom

375
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,450
如果那卫生间在天堂
if that bathroom is in heaven.

376
00:14:01,730 --> 00:14:03,300
很高兴你能来这里
I'm so glad you came back here.

377
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,240
我也是
Me too.

378
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,600
感觉很奇怪
This feels weird.

379
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,980
你有包间吗
Do you have a compartment?

380
00:14:09,710 --> 00:14:11,740
我有 但你要怎么过来呢
I do, but how will you get up there?

381
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:12,620
我会有办法的
I'll find a way.

382
00:14:13,370 --> 00:14:14,280
我答应你
I promise.

383
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:19,150
另外 我在18B间
Oh, by the way, I'm in compartment 18B,

384
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:21,410
也就是"男孩你太可爱了"
as in, "Boy, are you cute."

385
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:24,130
我真是傻 快走吧
Idiot. Just keep walking.

386
00:14:24,230 --> 00:14:25,000
可以了
Got it.

387
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,030
我有信号了
I have a signal.

388
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:27,770
-太好了 -各位 各位 别这样
- Oh, good. - Guys, guys, guys, come on.

389
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:29,970
我们唯一需要的信号是这个
The only signal we need is this.

390
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:32,180
我的孩子们 他们并不讨厌迪迪
My kids in the back -- they don't hate Dede.

391
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:34,100
他们在为婚礼准备烧烤
They're preparing a roast for the wedding.

392
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:35,580
那是我们家表达爱的方式
That's how our family shows love.

393
00:14:35,590 --> 00:14:37,380
你们会在宴会上尝到的
You'll get a taste of it at the reception.

394
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:38,330
你们是哪国人 意大利吗
What are you, Italian?

395
00:14:38,330 --> 00:14:39,470
我们会做全套的
We'll do a whole thing,

396
00:14:39,470 --> 00:14:40,930
除非你们学《教父》扫射现场
unless you shoot the place up first.

397
00:14:40,930 --> 00:14:42,490
看到没 就是这样
Oh. See? That kind of stuff.

398
00:14:42,490 --> 00:14:45,180
杰·普里契特 我要掐死你
Jay Pritchett, I am going to strangle you!

399
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,610
我不知道为什么你假装
I don't know why you're pretending

400
00:14:46,610 --> 00:14:47,640
你不认识我
that you don't know me,

401
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:50,340
但我敢肯定你是为了什么愚蠢又自私的理由
but I'm sure it's for some stupid and selfish reason!

402
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:51,650
她真的是你妻子吗
She really is your wife?

403
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:52,830
暂时是
For now.

404
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:54,770
很快 你就会坐上一辆
Pretty soon, you're gonna be getting on a train

405
00:14:54,770 --> 00:14:56,350
开往我下场婚礼的列车
to my next wedding.

406
00:14:56,350 --> 00:14:58,010
你快逼疯我了
You're driving me insane.

407
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,630
我懂了
Oh, I see what's going on.

408
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:00,540
别听她的
Don't listen to her.

409
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:03,000
迪迪并没有疯 你疯了
Dede's not crazy. You are.

410
00:15:03,190 --> 00:15:04,380
当然 也可以
Sure. That works.

411
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,470
你是谁
Who are you?

412
00:15:05,470 --> 00:15:06,300
我是卡尔
Oh, I'm Carl.

413
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:08,020
我父亲要跟迪迪结婚
Uh, my father's marrying Dede.

414
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:09,550
是的 他要结婚 一起庆祝吧
Yes, he is, and let's celebrate.

415
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:10,670
喝什么我买单
Drinks on me.

416
00:15:10,930 --> 00:15:11,490
没关系了
What the heck.

417
00:15:11,490 --> 00:15:13,790
再次 很抱歉我让你们担心迪迪的事
And, again, I'm sorry to have worried you guys about Dede.

418
00:15:13,790 --> 00:15:14,460
别这样
Oh, please.

419
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:16,710
卡尔的爸爸也不是什么善茬
It's not like Carl's father is such a prize.

420
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:18,000
怎么了
What?

421
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,640
他打砸抢烧了你妈妈的房子
He snapped and burned your mom's house down.

422
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:20,830
她在开玩笑
She's kidding.

423
00:15:20,830 --> 00:15:22,350
我们也准备了烧烤
Uh, we're doing a roast, too.

424
00:15:22,350 --> 00:15:24,660
是啊 你妈妈就差点变烧猪了
Yeah, right. Your mother was almost a roast.

425
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,630
我们要证明这场犯罪是可行的
We needed to prove that the crime was feasible,

426
00:15:30,630 --> 00:15:34,390
所以我要假扮工程师兼杀人犯的角色
so I would play the role of engineer/murderer.

427
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:36,470
而我要假扮其他所有人的角色
And I would play the role of everyone else.

428
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:39,060
我家乡剧院出品的《罗宾汉》
When my hometown theater's production of "Robin Hood"

429
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:41,470
缺女主演的时候 我除了扮演修士
was lacking a leading lady, I stepped into the role

430
00:15:41,470 --> 00:15:44,140
还顺带出演了一下女仆玛丽安的角色
of Maid Marian in addition to playing the Friar.

431
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:45,070
-塔克吗 -其实本没有必要
- Tuck? - Didn't have to.

432
00:15:45,070 --> 00:15:47,110
戏服掩饰得很好
The costume hid it quite nicely.

433
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,780
我周日了狗了
Sunday dinner!

434
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:54,540
什么
What?!

435
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:55,710
那个土耳其大使的保镖
The Turkish ambassador's bodyguard

436
00:15:55,710 --> 00:15:59,350
得到命令要干掉所有可疑人员
was instructed to neutralize anyone who looks suspicious.

437
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:01,580
什么
What?

438
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,030
土耳其语 从头开始的意思
It's Turkish for "From the top."

439
00:16:03,030 --> 00:16:04,960
你回来前我实在是太无聊了
I have a lot of downtime while you're resetting.

440
00:16:06,890 --> 00:16:07,680
汪
Woof!

441
00:16:08,130 --> 00:16:09,850
难道你忘了马克西姆·杜维纳伯爵
Did you forget Count Maxim du Vernay

442
00:16:09,850 --> 00:16:11,600
带了他的沙皮犬吗
brought his service Shar-pei?

443
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:14,310
说实话 那部分我没读
If I'm being honest, I skimmed that part.

444
00:16:14,310 --> 00:16:15,330
重来
Again!

445
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:22,670
你好 准备好了吗
Hi. You ready for me?

446
00:16:22,670 --> 00:16:24,990
我自认为已经查了所有该知道的东西
I believe I've Googled everything I need to know.

447
00:16:30,510 --> 00:16:33,100
那我们就开始吧
So, let's get started.

448
00:16:36,890 --> 00:16:38,310
这是加利福尼亚
This is California.

449
00:16:38,450 --> 00:16:42,010
苏必利尔湖在这里 横跨...
Lake Superior is here, all the way across --

450
00:16:42,010 --> 00:16:43,600
你在脱我的鞋吗
Are you trying to take off my shoe?

451
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,540
我以为你想给我看什么东西
I thought you wanted to show me things.

452
00:16:45,810 --> 00:16:46,660
是啊
I do.

453
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:50,700
我是个地理老师 孩子 你真需要补补课了
I'm a geography teacher, and, boy, do you need one.

454
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,400
开什么玩笑
Are you kidding me?

455
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:55,590
如果她的新丈夫是个纵火犯
If her new husband is an arsonist,

456
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:56,640
那你们必须告诉她
you guys have to tell her.

457
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,270
各位 冷静点 那家伙烧过一座房子
Everybody, calm down. The guy burned down one house.

458
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:02,410
他没进监狱 说明他在政府有人
He's not in jail, so he's got the government's A-okay.

459
00:17:02,410 --> 00:17:04,480
我最近发觉妈妈有点问题
I recently discovered I have some issues with Mom,

460
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,430
但我爱她
but I love her.

461
00:17:05,430 --> 00:17:06,920
我不希望她在一所燃烧的房子里醒来
I don't want her to wake up in a burning house

462
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,620
尽管她婚后你就不用再付赡养费了
just so you don't have to pay alimony.

463
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:11,150
我也爱妈妈 通常情况下
I love Mom, too... usually.

464
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:12,670
但如果婚礼取消
But if this wedding doesn't happen,

465
00:17:12,670 --> 00:17:14,860
你知道未来十年她会去哪
you know where she's gonna end up in 10 years --

466
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:18,040
不是你家就是我家
su casa or...my...casa.

467
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:21,210
而且 他的第一任妻子令他发了疯
Besides, the first wife obviously drove the guy nuts.

468
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:22,920
我们怎么知道你母亲...
How do we know your mother's gonna --

469
00:17:23,570 --> 00:17:25,150
老天
Oh, geez.

470
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:30,290
卢克 你学得可真快
Luke, you're such a quick learner.

471
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,040
谢谢 我原来不知道这地方就在那儿
Thanks. I had no idea that was there.

472
00:17:36,730 --> 00:17:37,490
请进
Come in.

473
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:41,700
是你吗
Is that you?

474
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,300
我马上就出来
I'll be out in a second.

475
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:46,190
真是太淘气了
This is so naughty.

476
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,390
我打算去见艾丽克斯 劝她放弃
I was going to see Alex and let her down easy.

477
00:17:48,390 --> 00:17:50,580
她是我的家人 这是乱伦
I mean, she's family. It's taboo.

478
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:51,670
对不起
I'm sorry.

479
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:55,850
我不该评头论足的 尤其是在火车上
I shouldn't be judgy, especially when, you know, trains.

480
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:02,100
真黑 我喜欢
Ooh. Dark. I like it.

481
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,420
我是来拒绝你的[失去性致]
I-I was going to let you down!

482
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:06,750
你做到了
You sure did!

483
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:09,860
你的帽子太显眼了
Well, your hat was garish.

484
00:18:10,450 --> 00:18:11,510
请问
Excuse me.

485
00:18:11,780 --> 00:18:12,810
你们中是否有人看见
Have any of you guys seen the guy

486
00:18:12,810 --> 00:18:14,280
刚才跟我一起跳舞的人
I was dancing with earlier?

487
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:17,810
结果是 我离开后詹姆斯就下车了
So, it turns out James got off right after I left him.

488
00:18:18,110 --> 00:18:21,240
说句题外话 我的钱包不见了
On a possibly unrelated note, my wallet is gone.

489
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:23,490
火车
Trains.

490
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,700
黑斯廷斯先生 我们做到了
Mr. Hastings, we did it.

491
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:28,860
我们到了厨房又回来了 没被别人发现
We made it to the caboose and back without being seen.

492
00:18:29,490 --> 00:18:30,350
你设计的情节是可行的
Your book works.

493
00:18:30,350 --> 00:18:31,940
真不敢相信 你们确定吗
I can't believe it. Are you sure?

494
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:34,590
-是的 -是的 结合了渺小 智慧和伪装
- Yes! - Yes. It's a combination of slithering, clever disguise,

495
00:18:34,590 --> 00:18:35,910
不是对您的写作提什么建议
and not to write the book for you,

496
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:37,830
但如果伯爵有只义肢 会很有帮助的
but it would help if the Count had a wooden hand.

497
00:18:37,830 --> 00:18:40,140
我也正有此意
Well, I was sort of in that area anyway.

498
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:42,270
真是万分感谢
A thousand thank-yous.

499
00:18:42,270 --> 00:18:43,540
锡尔弗敦活下来了
Silverton lives!

500
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,960
太棒了
Yay!

501
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:48,640
你们几个在研究书的事吧
Hi. Oh, you guys are doing that book thing, right?

502
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:50,800
-是啊 -不知道是否能帮上忙
- Yeah. - Well, I don't know if this helps at all,

503
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:52,470
不过刚才我跟司机谈过
but I was just talking to the engineer.

504
00:18:52,470 --> 00:18:54,020
结果是 他不能离开驾驶室
It turns out he can't leave the controls

505
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:56,420
因为那个叫驾驶失知制动装置的东西
because of what's called a dead man's switch.

506
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:59,190
如果他离开那里 整辆火车就会停下来
If he takes his foot off of it, the whole train stops.

507
00:18:59,190 --> 00:19:01,120
不用谢我
Anyway, you're welcome.

508
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:09,410
如果司机不能离开驾驶室 那么...
If the engineer can't leave the controls, then...

509
00:19:09,410 --> 00:19:10,880
他就不能实施谋杀
He can't commit the murder.

510
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,010
结束了
It's over.

511
00:19:12,010 --> 00:19:14,380
黑斯廷斯 我们很抱歉
Hastings, we are so sorry.

512
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,670
是时候摆脱这
It's time to rid myself

513
00:19:16,670 --> 00:19:19,490
五百页的废纸了
of this 500-hundred page stain.

514
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:20,690
等等 不要
Wait! No! No, no, no, no!

515
00:19:20,690 --> 00:19:21,930
-不 不要 -该死 怎么打不开
- No! No, no! - Open, damn you!

516
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:23,030
等等
Wait! Wait!

517
00:19:23,030 --> 00:19:24,810
那是火车尾吗
Is that the back of the train?

518
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:29,240
没错 这就是著名的"马蹄转角"
Yep. This is the famous horseshoe turn.

519
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,550
在美国境内只有两处
Only two of them in the continental United States,

520
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:33,350
其中一处就是在加利福尼亚
one of which is here in California,

521
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:34,920
而加利福尼亚在北美
which is in North America.

522
00:19:35,130 --> 00:19:37,170
呜呼哀哉 现在我都知道了
Sadly, I know all of this now.

523
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:38,720
就是这
That's it.

524
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:41,020
司机从没离开驾驶室
The engineer -- he never has to leave the controls.

525
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:42,830
他等到了马蹄转角
He waits for the horseshoe turn.

526
00:19:42,830 --> 00:19:45,000
就把伯爵一枪干死在最后一节车厢里
Then he plugs the Earl in the caboose.

527
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:45,690
听起来有点怪
I heard it.

528
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:47,400
这简直太秒了
This is brilliant!

529
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,950
真不敢相信你们两个小丑救了我的书
I can't believe you two clowns have saved my book.

530
00:19:50,950 --> 00:19:53,180
其实 只有我是小丑
Actually, it's just one clown.

531
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:54,520
我是魔术师
One magician.

532
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:57,730
-老妈 -好啊 老妈
- Hey, Mom! Hi! - Hi, Mom!

533
00:19:57,730 --> 00:19:59,860
原有的家人们 你们好
Well, hello, original family.

534
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:01,640
迪迪 我们有事要告诉你
Dede, we have something we have to tell you.

535
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,530
我知道有更委婉的方式可以用
Now, I know there's a delicate way to say this.

536
00:20:03,530 --> 00:20:05,090
只不过我没去想
Just can't think of it.

537
00:20:05,110 --> 00:20:07,190
你的未婚夫是个纵火犯
Your fiancé's a pyro.

538
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:09,680
他烧了他前妻的房子
He burnt down his ex-wife's house.

539
00:20:09,950 --> 00:20:13,440
你们三个就想毁了我的好日子
It's just like you three to try to ruin my big day.

540
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,280
妈妈 我们认为你应该知道
Mom, we just thought you should know.

541
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,800
杰瑞什么都告诉我了
Jerry told me everything.

542
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,410
相信我 那个女人罪有应得
Trust me. She had it coming.

543
00:20:18,410 --> 00:20:19,930
那女人是个疯子
The woman's "Cah-razy."

544
00:20:19,930 --> 00:20:21,880
所以你不介意他是个纵火犯吗
So, you're okay he's a firebug?

545
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,740
他充满激情 杰
He's passionate, Jay.

546
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:27,330
他知道该怎么宣泄自己的情感 不像你
He knows how to express his feelings, unlike you.

547
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:29,300
如果你也能烧了我们的房子
Maybe if you had burned our house down,

548
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:30,920
或许我们现在还在一起
we'd still be together.

549
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:32,550
是我的错 你说得对 迪迪
My mistake. You're right, Dede.

550
00:20:32,550 --> 00:20:34,030
很好 妈妈 婚礼上见
Great, Mom. See you at the wedding.

551
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:35,850
再见 克莱尔 我为你安排的座位
Bye. Claire, you're not mad at me

552
00:20:35,850 --> 00:20:37,710
你不会生气吧
about your seating arrangements?

553
00:20:37,710 --> 00:20:38,770
为什么生气 我坐在哪里
Why? Where am I sitting?

554
00:20:38,770 --> 00:20:39,850
米奇尔 你来告诉她
Mitchell, tell her.

555
00:20:39,850 --> 00:20:40,970
我挂了
Got to run.

556
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,940
你不会坐在家人桌上
You're not sitting at the family table.

557
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,260
记好咯
Hello!

558
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:49,310
菲尔寄给我他的锡尔弗敦同人小说
Phil sent me his Silverton fan fiction,

559
00:20:49,310 --> 00:20:51,270
《开放日·密闭之棺》
"Open House, Closed Casket."

560
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:53,520
他抬头看见这伟大房间中
"He looked up at the pristine crown molding

561
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:55,210
原本的天花板线 呼吸到
in the great room and felt the breeze

562
00:20:55,210 --> 00:20:57,380
刚修缮过的中央空调中排放出的空气
of the recently updated central air.

563
00:20:57,380 --> 00:21:01,020
克拉泽斯夫人 在这令人向往的小房里
'Mrs. Coruthers, just as this desirable corner lot

564
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:05,380
被劈成两半了 克拉泽斯先生亦是如此
was split in half, so, too, is Mr. Coruthers.'

565
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:07,230
寡妇喘着气靠在
The widow gasped and steadied herself

566
00:21:07,230 --> 00:21:09,440
花岗岩厨房岛旁 恰如其分地表现出
on the granite kitchen island, a fitting metaphor

567
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,370
她内心的孤独感 尽管她正路过
for how alone she felt, despite being walking distance

568
00:21:12,370 --> 00:21:15,900
生机勃勃的商业区和优秀的学校
to a vibrant shopping district and wonderful schools."

569
00:21:16,390 --> 00:21:18,800
这两周我一直在躲着他
I've been avoiding him for the last two weeks.

570
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:39,060
别接电话
Don't answer that!
